    <section id="d120b-the-xml-and-xhtml-output-methods-packet-3-3">
      <title>D120b. The XML and XHTML output methods (packet <ref kind="packet" to="3.3"/>)</title>
      <p>Recorded 2026-10-17 as a second <ref kind="decision" to="D120"/> (4.3 has <ref kind="decision" to="D120"/>); renamed at the Phase 2 gate (<ref kind="decision" to="D151"/>). <code>src/serialize_internal.h</code> splits the serializer into parts: <code>src/serialize.c</code> keeps the output stream and buffer, the parameter checks, the character pipeline, sequence normalization, the adaptive method and the dispatch; <code>src/serialize_xml.c</code> has the XML and XHTML methods and the node writer the adaptive method uses. Packet <ref kind="packet" to="3.4"/>'s HTML, text, JSON and CSV parts build on the same internal interface.</p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p><strong>Dispatch</strong> (<ref kind="decision" to="D106"/> follow-up): HTML, text, JSON and CSV return UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE until 3.4; parameters C can say but XDM cannot (enumerations out of range, ill-formed UTF-8, name 0, a character map codepoint twice or not an XML Char) are INVALID_ARGUMENT for every method; indent-unit, doctype-system, doctype-public and html-version values the spec forbids are SEPM0016.</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p><strong>Character pipeline</strong> (Serialization 4.0, section 4): <code>sxml_serializer</code> writes markup, text, attribute values, URI attribute values and CDATA sections. Text and attribute values go through the character map (sorted once, binary search), then <code>sxml_unicode_normalize</code> (<ref kind="decision" to="D107"/>; the serialize.h form maps onto unicode_internal.h's, fully-normalized as NFC plus SERE0012 for a construct that starts with a composing character) on each unmapped segment, then escaping, line endings and the encoding into a 512-byte staging area. References are <code>&amp;#xHEX;</code>; C0 and C1 controls, NEL and LINE SEPARATOR are always references in text and attributes (also with version 1.0: XML 1.1's repertoire, QT4 K2-Serialization-7, Serialization-xml-27 to -31); a character the encoding lacks is a reference there and SERE0008 in markup. UTF-16 is big endian; byte-order-mark writes EF BB BF or FE FF.</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p><strong>Sequence normalization</strong> is a pull iterator (<code>sxml_sequence_normalizer</code>) that never builds the result tree: frames flatten arrays and JNode values, atomic items are cast to text joined by a space or the item separator, documents give their children, text is merged in a heap buffer. SEPM0004 (doctype-system or standalone with text or several elements at the top) runs the iterator once more first.</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p><strong>Namespaces</strong>: each element's declarations are computed against a stack of written bindings: its in-scope namespaces (minus xml) plus what its own and its attributes' names need, declared where the written bindings differ, <code>xmlns=""</code> where a default goes out of scope, and <code>xmlns:p=""</code> only with undeclare-prefixes and version 1.1 (SEPM0010 with 1.0). XHTML with HTML5 applies prefix normalization (XHTML, SVG, MathML elements unprefixed; their prefixes dropped unless an attribute of an ancestor-or-self uses them, Issue 2821). Canonical XML uses the same rule (it is C14N 1.1's namespace axis) and sorts declarations and attributes by heapsort (no recursion, O(n log n)).</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p><strong>Indentation</strong> (5.1.4, 6.1.5): an element's content is indented only when it has element, comment or PI children and no text other than whitespace, its name is not in suppress-indentation (XHTML: also without regard to case), it has no xml:space="preserve", it is not a formatted or inline HTML element and has no inline child, and its parent is indented itself, so nothing below mixed or suppressed content moves. Whitespace-only text is dropped where whitespace is added. indent-unit defaults to two spaces; indent-attributes puts each further attribute on its own line. Newlines between top-level nodes and after the declaration only when indenting; none otherwise (QT4 Serialization-xml-01, -xhtml-72).</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p><strong>XHTML</strong> (section 6): html-version defaults to 5.0; minimized tags only for elements expected to be empty (<code>&lt;br/&gt;</code> with HTML5, <code>&lt;br /&gt;</code> before), <code>&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</code> otherwise; <code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</code> before an html document element with HTML5 and no doctype-system; include-content-type (default yes) adds <code>&lt;meta charset="ENC"/&gt;</code> (HTML5) or the http-equiv form (media type text/html by default) as head's first child and drops existing charset or Content-Type meta children; escape-uri-attributes (default yes) applies URI escaping to the attributes of appendix D.</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p><strong>Canonical XML</strong>: UTF-8, LF, no declaration, doctype, CDATA, character maps or indentation; start-end tag pairs; line feeds around nodes outside the document element; SERE0024 for top-level text, more or fewer than one element, or a relative namespace URI.</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p><strong>Adaptive nodes</strong> (<ref kind="decision" to="D82"/>) are written by the same XML writer with the default parameters; a stored parentless namespace node (<ref kind="decision" to="D98"/>) is written from its name (the prefix) and content (the URI).</p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>Not done here: <code>sxml_serialization_parameter_reader</code> (declared by <ref kind="decision" to="D106"/>) has no definition yet; it belongs with fn:serialize (3.4). Not checked: SERE0005/SERE0006 (names and characters of the XML version), comments with "--" (SERE0003). The CLI's <code>--method</code> stays adaptive until 3.12.</p>
        </item>
      </list>
